BANK1.FAQ         Frequently asked questions

The Advanced Options Module 1 offers you the following additional functions:

    Look Ahead Mode to predict the state of your finances sometime in the future.
    Default Transactions for those regular entries.
    A ‘Last Transaction Repeat’ function
    A pull-down page of Account details where you can store such things as Account numbers.
    Automatic numbering (for cheques, or in my case registrations !)
    A ‘Find’ function in the Archive screen.

The Advanced Options Module 2 offers you the following additional functions:

    Export and Import function in various formats, including Quicken.
    A ‘Pay Bills’ option, similar to that used in MS Money. (Also needs BANKORD.OVL)
    Ability to allocate tax (VAT, GST etc) to transactions.
    Pull-down Info windows giving settings for each Group and Account.

The Optional Configuration Module allows you to change a large number of the settings within the program.  These settings are remembered, so you can remove this module once the program is setup to your liking.

To Install the program, carry out the following actions:

1.    Copy SNABANK1.APP to your \APP\ directory.

2.    If you wish to load any of the optional modules, generate a Sub-directory \SNABANK\ under the \APP\ directory, i.e. \APP\SNABANK\

3.    You can then copy any of the optional files to the sub-directory  \APP\SNABANK\ if you wish to use any of the extra facilities.

4.    If you want to use the optional Print system, as well as copying the file BANKSPRT.OVL into the \APP\SNABANK\ Sub-directory, you will need to put the SNAPRINT.DYL file into an \OPD\ directory. (Note that this latter file is common to all my programs, so if you are running more than one of them, you will only need one copy of this file)

5.    Install SNABANK1.APP using <PSION-I> as described in the Psion manual.

If you fancy a challenge, you can learn everything you need to about the program by playing with it and checking the effect of each MENU selection, as well as the effect of pressing <ENTER>, <DELETE>, <TAB> or <ESC> in each screen.  However, PLEASE, PLEASE, PLEASE, at least read Part 1 of this set of instructions first. I suggest you then work through the tutorial in Part 2, which will familiarize you with all the basic capabilities of the program.  If you do 'fly blind' and get into trouble, please read the rest of this document before asking me to help.  The majority of questions I receive could have been answered by reading this document.  Those that couldn’t I have included in the FAQ file.

If you do get a problem, PLEASE read the full instructions.  I have yet to be asked a question that wasn't already fully explained in the instructions or the FAQ file !!

